Here are the fixes to ensure the **Branch Search strictly only looks at the Branch Code**, and the **Helper Texts perfectly disappear** as soon as the user enters data.
### 1. Restrict Branch Search to Code Only
Since the backend API might be returning matches for both the name and the code, we can add a strict filter on the frontend to instantly drop any results that don't match the Branch Code.
**Find your searchBranches function (around line 185) and update it to this:**
```javascript
  const searchBranches = useCallback(
    debounce(async (query, rowId) => {
      if (!query || query.trim().length < 3) {
        setBranchSearch({ loadingId: null, options: [] });
        return;
      }
      setBranchSearch((prev) => ({ ...prev, loadingId: rowId }));
      try {
        const response = await callApi(
          `/JS/branches-journal/search?query=${encodeURIComponent(query)}`,
          null,
          "GET"
        );

        // --- NEW: Strictly filter out any results where the CODE doesn't match the query ---
        // This completely prevents searching by branch name!
        const filteredOptions = (response || []).filter((opt) => 
          opt.code && opt.code.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase())
        );

        setBranchSearch({ loadingId: null, options: filteredOptions });
      } catch (error) {
        showSnackBar("Branch search failed.", "error");
        setBranchSearch({ loadingId: null, options: [] });
      }
    }, 300),
    [callApi, showSnackBar]
  );

```
